internal/monty vendors the Go wrapper and the Rust WASM shim for the Pydantic
Monty Python interpreter. Monty itself (https://github.com/pydantic/monty)
is distributed under the MIT License; the LICENSE files in this directory
and in shim/ are upstream's and apply here rather than the repository-root
licence.

Hard fork, September 2026. Upstream fugue-labs/monty-go (v0.2.0, commit
c5fede1ca39482ff3da7dc04c5fd569b8bc313b8) was the source of everything in
this directory; it is treated as frozen at that commit and will not be
pulled from again. Upstream development has stalled, and the wrapper is
small enough — three Go files plus a ~850-line Rust shim — that owning it
outright costs less than tracking a dormant dependency.

  * monty.go, wasm.go, errors.go — the Go wrapper (wazero plumbing,
    pause/resume for external function calls). The package name was
    rewritten from `montygo` to `monty` and error strings from `montygo: …`
    to `monty: …`; otherwise upstream verbatim as of the fork commit.
  * shim/ — the Rust shim (crates/monty-wasm) that exposes Monty's
    pause/resume API as the C-ABI WASM exports the Go wrapper drives,
    built against pydantic/monty v0.0.21. It is a hard fork of the shim
    upstream shipped for monty v0.0.11, with the v0.0.21 API adaptation
    described in shim/README.md.
  * monty.wasm — the built shim, embedded by monty.go. Rebuilt with
    `make -C shim check`; reproducible, see shim/README.md.

The fork is the maintenance point now. Changes to the shim land here, are
committed here, and are described in shim/README.md as changes to make —
written so a future session can re-derive them against a newer pydantic/monty
tag without needing the upstream repository at all. Upgrading the pinned
pydantic/monty tag is the one thing that still reaches outside this tree;
bump the two git dependencies in shim/crates/monty-wasm/Cargo.toml and
follow shim/README.md.

The Go wrapper's only dependencies are github.com/tetratelabs/wazero (pure
Go) and golang.org/x/sys, both already in the repository's go.mod. The shim
builds against the pydantic/monty git crate; see shim/README.md for the
reproducibility nuance that carries with that.
